The units with large weights mostly track the specified inputs. Unit 0 responds to x14 and x26 together, unit 1 is suppressed by x3 and x29, and unit 4 combines x3, x14, x26 and x29. Unit 16 is an exception: it is dense, with sizeable weights on many inputs (x0, x1, x4, x10, x11, x12, x24, x25, and others). I could not tell from the weights whether it implements a rare backdoor trigger or is just training noise. A hidden trigger would have to be a sharp conjunction of many bits, and nothing in the biases I checked clearly forms one.

